fingerprint and so puts every stored crypto byte anchor back under review.
Re-attestation adds no evidence by itself, so here is the argument, checked
rather than asserted:

* 19 of the 20 `cryptoAxiomPending` fixtures are STATELESS. A stateless
  contract emits no `check_preimage`, so the binding blob never appears in its
  script and a change to that constant cannot move its hex. Verified by
  scanning each fixture's `expected-ir.json` for a `check_preimage` node
  rather than inferring it from the names.

* The one stateful fixture, `state-covenant`, DID move -- and its `.regenLive`
  anchor was regenerated for the new construction, not carried over. Its
  stored constant is 864 bytes, is byte-identical to
  `conformance/tests/state-covenant/expected-script.hex`, and CONTAINS the
  428-byte Any-S blob verbatim. That golden is independently justified:
  reproduced by all seven tiers (conformance runner 72/72) and pinned in
  `conformance/golden-provenance-allowlist.json`.

So the fingerprint literal was the only stale thing; no anchor is re-blessed
without having been re-derived under the model it now names.

RE-ATTESTED AGAIN 2026-09-08, for the post-Genesis operand-width repair in
`Stack.Eval.asNum?` (it used to reject byte vectors wider than 4 bytes -- the
PRE-Genesis CScriptNum limit -- which is not the chain this project targets).

This one is structural rather than per-fixture, and therefore stronger than
the argument above. `asNum?` is an EVALUATOR-side operand coercion. The
stored crypto byte anchors record LOWERED hex, and lowering cannot reach the
evaluator: `RunarVerification/Stack/Lower.lean` does not import
`Stack/Eval.lean` and contains zero references to `asNum?`. There is no path
from this change to any lowered byte, for any fixture, so no anchor can have
moved -- rather than 20 separate claims about 20 fixtures, this is one claim
about the dependency graph, and it is checkable with grep.

Corroborated by the run: the byte-exact count is 58/74 both before and after
the change, and every bucket size is unchanged.
