Finding #6 — INERT crypto byte-anchor inventory (enforced TODO).

The default-mode `pipelineGolden` gate is the "second-implementation byte
anchor": for each `cryptoAxiomPending` fixture it compares a stored Lean
`compileHex` constant (`cryptoAxiomPendingExpected`) against
`expected-script.hex`. A stored constant is INERT when it provides no genuine
cross-check — either **unpopulated** (`none`, never regenerated) or **stale**
(present but disagreeing with the current golden). Previously the gate skipped
both cases SILENTLY (unpopulated → non-fatal NOTICE, stale → dropped with no
output at all), so a crypto byte anchor could go dark unnoticed and the
low-friction "fix" for a red gate was to PASTE `expected-script.hex` into the
constant (making the anchor permanently tautological).

This list names EVERY currently-inert crypto anchor. `main` now enforces that
the live inert set (unpopulated ∪ stale) EXACTLY equals this inventory:
  * a crypto anchor that goes inert WITHOUT being listed here fails the gate
    (a previously-live anchor silently drifted — investigate the codegen
    change, do NOT paste the golden); and
  * a name listed here that is no longer inert fails the gate (its constant now
    matches the golden — remove it in a reviewed change, and confirm via
    `RUNAR_VERIFICATION_REGEN=1` that the constant was regenerated LIVE, not
    pasted, before trusting the anchor).

Populating an entry (turning it from a gap into a live anchor) requires the
multi-hour offline crypto regen — see the header docstring and the
`runar-verification-regen.yml` anti-paste workflow (`workflow_dispatch`).
Count: 18 (cryptoAxiomPending minus the three 2026-09 live anchors
`babybear`, `merkle-proof`, `state-covenant` whose compileHexSafe now
matches the goldens after the R-119 / R-120 / R-095 ports).
-/
